-- title:
--   A completed defect has exactly one pair's worth of labels per index
-- statement:
--   Let $G=[n]\times\{0,1\}$ be the paired ground set, with Boolean labels written as $0,1$. A state is a subset of $G$. Let $\sigma:[n]\to\{\mathrm{unassigned},0,1\}$ be a partial assignment and let $e,f\in[n]$ be distinct empty and full pair indices. Form $D(\sigma;e,f)$ by selecting no label at $e$, both labels at $f$, and exactly the assigned label at every other pair, using label $0$ when unassigned. Then $$|D(\sigma;e,f)|=n.$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/OmittedRankWeightPolynomial.lean#L84-L109

